# GUIShop Worth Display System

The worth display system shows item sell values in the item lore, updated in real-time via packets.

## Requires
- **PacketEvents** library (optional dependency)
- Enabled in `worth.yml`

## Key Classes

### WorthDisplayManager (`src/com/pablo67340/guishop/worth/`)
- Manages packet listeners for worth lore injection
- Handles SET_SLOT and WINDOW_ITEMS packets
- Modifies item lore client-side only (no server-side changes)

### Worth Configuration (`worth.yml`)
```yaml
enabled: true
format: "&7Worth: &a$%worth%"
hide-armor-slots: true  # Don't show worth on equipped armor
inventory-title-blacklist:  # Inventories to skip
  - "Auction House"
  - "Crate"
item-name-blacklist:  # Items with these name patterns get no worth
  - "Backpack"
  - "Kit"
```

## How It Works

1. **Packet Interception:**
   - Listens for SET_SLOT and WINDOW_ITEMS packets
   - Modifies items BEFORE sending to client

2. **Worth Lookup:**
   - Checks `GUIShop.getITEMTABLE()` for sell price
   - Uses item material + optional NBT matching

3. **Lore Injection:**
   - Appends worth line to existing lore
   - Only visual (client-side), original item unchanged

## API Hook

Other plugins can disable worth for specific players:
```java
GUIShopAPI.setExternalWorthCheck(player -> {
    return myPlugin.hasWorthDisabled(player);
});
```

## Player Toggle Command
```
/gs toggleworth - Toggles worth display for the player (session only)
```

## Armor Slot Handling

When `hide-armor-slots: true`, worth is stripped from equipped armor (slots 5-8):
- Uses `stripWorthFromPacketItem()` to actively REMOVE existing worth lore
- Not just skipping processing - must strip because items may already have lore

## Inventory Blacklist Matching

Blacklisted inventories use normalized title comparison:
```java
private String stripForComparison(String input) {
    // Fix UTF-8 encoding issues (Â§ -> §)
    // Strip hex color codes: §x§f§3§9§c§1§2
    // Strip standard color codes: §a, &b, etc.
    // Keep only letters, digits, spaces
    // Lowercase and trim
}
```

This handles complex titles with unicode and color codes.

### Auto-Blacklisting GUIShop Inventories

GUIShop automatically blacklists its own inventory titles:
- All shop names from `shops/*.yml`
- Menu title from `menu.yml`
- Transaction GUI title
- Sell GUI title
- Value GUI title

This is done in `ConfigManager.autoBlacklistGuiShopInventories()` on plugin enable.

## Common Issues

**Worth not showing:**
- Check PacketEvents is installed
- Check `worth.yml` enabled: true
- Check item is registered in ITEMTABLE (has sell price in shop)

**Worth showing in wrong inventories:**
- Add inventory title to blacklist in worth.yml
- Blacklist uses normalized matching - just use the readable text

**Worth on equipped armor:**
- Set `hide-armor-slots: true` in worth.yml
- All 4 armor slots (5-8) are handled for helmet, chestplate, leggings, boots

**Worth in Creative Mode:**
- Worth display works in creative inventory
- Special CREATIVE_INVENTORY_ACTION packet handler adds worth to items taken from creative
- updateInventory() calls are skipped for creative players to prevent desync

**Folia TickThread errors:**
- `inventory.getHolder()` cannot be called on async threads in Folia
- `shouldSkipPlayerInventory()` checks `Bukkit.isPrimaryThread()` first
- If on async thread, returns false (allows worth processing to continue)
